      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "1. What is Type 1 Hypervisor?"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "type1-type2-hypervisor.webp",
      "caption": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A type 1 hypervisor, also called a bare-metal hypervisor, is software that installs directly onto physical hardware. It manages virtual machines without needing a host operating system. It gives peak speed and strong security for business data centers."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "2. Why Arch Linux."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "arch.webp",
      "caption": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "3. Check Hypervisor Support"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "URL",
      "code": "lscpu | grep -i Virtualization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "VT-x for Intel, AMD-Vi for AMD"
    },
